INSERT INTO characters (slug,name,team,creator,owner_id,tags,appears_in,data,status,url_slug,created_at,updated_at) VALUES
('astrologer','Astrologer','townsfolk','Goodpart',NULL,NULL,'The Menagerie','{"slug":"astrologer","name":"Astrologer","team":"townsfolk","ability":"On your first night, learn three statements. Once per game, at night, you learn if any have become true.","creator":"Goodpart","appearsIn":"The Menagerie","quote":"Who are we to believe we know better than the cosmos?","lede":"The Astrologer receives portents of events to come, and learns when one has come to pass.","howToRun":["Statements should relate to the game in some fashion, and can either be straightforward or cryptic, depending on how you wish to run the character. If the Astrologer is sober, at least one of the statements should be something that could happen during the game.","Reminder tokens are provided in order to mark notable events if they should be linked to a specific character or player."],"tips":["Firstly, the statements you learn may potentially hint towards things that could happen during the game, so that alone may serve as valuable information to the town.","But, more importantly, if you ever wake to learn a \"yes\", now you know that something you learned has indeed come to pass! Now it''s time to puzzle out what may have happened based on existing information, and using that information to help solve the game state.","Alternatively, you may never learn a yes, meaning that none of the three things you learned have come to pass - and that can potentially be equally useful."],"bluffing":["Bluffing as the Astrologer requires a bit of work ahead of time, but can wreak havoc if you convince town that your statements are legitimate. Make predictions about events that could - but will never - come to pass in this game. Town will likely work with your statements when given, and then once you drop the \"yes\" on them, town will likely scramble for days to try to figure out what it could mean. Crucially, noting that you''ve not yet received confirmation may be a good cause to keep you alive.","Alternatively, you may want to be truthful in your predictions, and dissuade town from those notions once it''s revealed that you''re evil. If you''re in a town that may be quick to discover what you really are, this could be an equally effective strategy!"],"fighting":[],"examples":["Laura is the Astrologer. They receive the following on Night 1:","\"Outsiders kissing\"","\"Tie a bow around the Demon\"","\"Surrounded by evil\"","On Night 3, Laura learns a yes. One of the above statements has come to pass, and the town intuits that the Fang Gu may have jumped to the Sweetheart.","George is the Imp bluffing as the Astrologer. They give the following statements:","\"A Minion dies at night\"","\"Protection from death\"","\"Neighbouring the Demon\"","George sinks a kill on Night 4, and \"learns\" a yes the same night, confirming their Minion who is bluffing as the Monk."],"firstNight":47,"firstNightReminder":"Give the Astrologer three statements about the game. Nod or shake your head depending on whether any of the Astrologer''s statements have come true.","otherNight":55,"otherNightReminder":"Nod or shake your head depending on whether any of the Astrologer''s statements have come true.","reminders":["1","2","3"],"setup":false,"image":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/astg.png","curata":false,"imageAlt":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/aste.png","customBoxes":[{"title":"Credit","content":"Additional credit: Vyvvyx"}]}','published','the-menagerie/astrologer',datetime('now'),datetime('now')),
('banker-the-menagerie','Banker','townsfolk','Goodpart',NULL,NULL,'The Menagerie','{"slug":"banker-the-menagerie","name":"Banker","team":"townsfolk","ability":"You start knowing three characters: one is in play.","creator":"Goodpart","appearsIn":"The Menagerie","quote":"Resumes lie; medical records lie; but bank records can be trusted. Even the devil needs somewhere to put their money that isn''t a sock drawer.","lede":"The Banker learns roles in play, but only one of them is real.","howToRun":["STs can give any three roles that are valid. You can provide three good roles, up to two evil roles, Outsiders, etc: all are suitable depending on the game state."],"tips":["As a first day info role, you are spent immediately, but unlike a lot of first day roles, you may want to hold on to your information until later in the game. As roles are slowly outed, you''ll be able to parse out which role is out-of-play, and with some confirmation, perhaps you can figure out which role was seen as a bluff! Inversely, holding on to your information may frame you unnecessarily, so giving your information to a trusted player early might help ensure your account can be relied upon.","Additionally, if you receive evil roles as part of your info, you can potentially deduce what role may be in, or out of play."],"bluffing":["If you''re bluffing as the Banker, you already know a Demon bluff - yours. Providing any three roles can frame certain worlds, but if you have a Minion such as a Scarlet Woman, you could even frame your own Demon to gain credibility. Your information is powerful, and obviously, subject to change depending on the world you want to build.","If you want to put an evil character in the three that you learn, you can frame certain Minions or Demons as being either in-play or not-in-play: this might lead town to build worlds around your information, and lead them to incorrect conclusions!"],"fighting":[],"examples":["Penny is the sober healthy Banker. She sees the Steward, the Empath, and the Fortune Teller. All three roles are claimed by other players, suggesting that one of the three is the role they claim, another is bluffing an out-of-play role, and one is evil.","Mitch is the Baron bluffing as the Banker. He says he sees the Poppy Grower, the Pixie, and the No Dashii. A No Dashii is in play, and knows that a Poppy Grower is not. The Pixie may, as a result, be lead to believe that the demon is not a No Dashii."],"firstNight":47,"firstNightReminder":"Show the Banker three characters.","otherNight":0,"otherNightReminder":"","reminders":[],"setup":false,"image":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/bang.png","curata":false,"imageAlt":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/bane.png"}','published','the-menagerie/banker',datetime('now'),datetime('now')),
('cartographer-the-menagerie','Cartographer','townsfolk','Goodpart',NULL,NULL,'The Menagerie','{"slug":"cartographer-the-menagerie","name":"Cartographer","team":"townsfolk","ability":"You start knowing two players: one is in the longest line of good players.","creator":"Goodpart","appearsIn":"The Menagerie","quote":"Live your life by a compass, not a clock.","lede":"The Cartographer learns where the majority of good players might reside.","howToRun":["Characters that misregister, such as the Recluse or Spy, can impact the Cartographer''s information."],"tips":["Find your line! This is essential especially if the number of adjacent good players is a large one, so finding the chunk of players who are more likely to be trusted than not is of great help to town. This is a role that can easily extract claims from players if your number seems reliable, so you can serve as a valuable conduit for information, and create confirmations around your own information.","Remember that Outsiders count as good players, but Outsiders that cause misregistration such as the Spy or Recluse can corrupt your information. Keep this in mind when putting together worlds."],"bluffing":["There are two ways to bluff as the Cartographer: you can either include yourself and perhaps Minions in the longest line of \"good\" players - or alternatively, you might consider placing the line where it actually is to lend credence to your bluff, especially if you know that certain roles will be able to confirm other good players. Just because the number is accurate doesn''t mean you can''t shift the line slightly to include those you need to protect."],"fighting":[],"examples":["Danny is the Cartographer who learns two players, one of which is himself. Near him is the Grandmother confirming a nearby player, and a neighbour dies at night. It is likely that Danny is in the longest line of good players.","Kris is the Assassin, bluffing as the Cartographer. He notes that the longest line of good players includes the Scarlet Woman. The Scarlet Woman proceeds to push on those outside of the line, including the Demon."],"firstNight":47,"firstNightReminder":"Show the Cartographer two players.","otherNight":0,"otherNightReminder":"","reminders":[],"setup":false,"image":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/carg.png","curata":false,"imageAlt":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/care.png"}','published','the-menagerie/cartographer',datetime('now'),datetime('now')),
('chameleon-the-menagerie','Chameleon','townsfolk','Goodpart',NULL,NULL,'The Menagerie','{"slug":"chameleon-the-menagerie","name":"Chameleon","team":"townsfolk","ability":"Each night, you gain a new ability and learn two characters it could belong to. Once per game, the ability is that of an Outsider or Minion.","creator":"Goodpart","appearsIn":"The Menagerie","quote":"Every person has their own shape, shade and hue. I am all of them.","lede":"The Chameleon sheds its role each night for something new, but may gain something unfavourable in the process.","howToRun":["Balance the Chameleon''s ability around how town is faring: selecting the best ability or abilities from available roles based on whether the Chameleon''s team is winning ensures the character helps their team while still feeling balanced.","Try to give the Chameleon \"pairs\" of roles that prompt similarly, even if the resulting information is different. The Fortune Teller, Innkeeper and Harpy; the Monk, Poisoner and Lycanthrope; the Ravenkeeper, Farmer and Klutz would be valid groups to select from on any given night.","If the Chameleon''s team needs a boost, you could consider giving it two roles that aren''t compatible in terms of picking and choosing, to guide the Chameleon towards the role they''re likely selecting for. You may also want to do this more frequently if the Chameleon is poisoned or drunk.","Note that with Demons that cause \"incorrect\" information like the Vortox, Chronos or Baku, the Chameleon learns correct roles, if not correct info."],"tips":["Determining which role you have gained each night is essential in decoding your information. A 2 on Night 1 could be a Chef, but it could be a Clockmaker. A 1 on Night 3 could be an Oracle, but it could be an Empath. Triangulate your varied info with that from the town around you in order to make sense of what you have on hand.","You always know which roles you might be gaining information for, so even if you don''t receive information, or wake at all, you can be reasonably assured that you are doing something. It''s simply your job to know what.","Remember that once per game, you will be given a Minion or Outsider ability, and it''s likely you won''t know the repercussion of that until it''s too late. So be up front with anyone you might adversely affect, prove that you''re worth trusting, and hopefully you can keep the damage to a minimum. Better yet - if you believe you''ve picked up a Minion''s ability, why not use it for good, and point it towards those you think are evil?"],"bluffing":["As the Chameleon, you can craft amazing worlds with a bevy of information from all over the script. Want to make up a Steward ping? You got it. Want to imply that perhaps you were the Lycanthrope who got a kill last night? No problem. Nothing is too farfetched, as long as you sound credible.","At all times, your role is masked with ambiguity, so making fake claims isn''t necessarily an admission of evil - just that you might not be receiving the information you think you are. Push on your info to best suit the world you need to build, and don''t worry, because you''re always able to change your role the next day.","Better yet, if you can coordinate your movements with any in-play Minions, you can even mimic the night you receive an evil ability. If you''ve made someone Cerenovus mad, let them know it was you to build trust!"],"fighting":[],"examples":["Judy is the Chameleon. She learns the roles Chef and Empath on Night 1. She learns Devil''s Advocate or Monk on Night 2, and is asked to pick a player. She chooses the Oracle, who dies during the night. On Night 3, she learns Artist or Ravenkeeper, and receives no further prompts.","Jake is the Vortox, bluffing as the Chameleon. He pretends to send a Nightwatchman ping to his Minion, and tells them to pretend that it was instead sent by the other Minion. On Night 2, he kills the Town Crier and says that he was told he could be the Lycanthrope or the Acrobat, selecting the Town Crier, who died. Jake feigns surprise as he assumes he must have picked up the Lycanthrope''s ability."],"firstNight":15,"firstNightReminder":"Assign the Chameleon''s character and wake the Chameleon at the point in the night order corresponding to that character. Show the Chameleon two characters prior to any further effects.","otherNight":29,"otherNightReminder":"Assign the Chameleon''s character and wake the Chameleon at the point in the night order corresponding to that character. Show the Chameleon two characters prior to any further effects.","reminders":["1","2","3","4","Minion","Outsider"],"setup":false,"image":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/chamg.png","curata":false,"imageAlt":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/chame.png"}','published','the-menagerie/chameleon',datetime('now'),datetime('now')),
('cleric-the-menagerie','Cleric','townsfolk','Goodpart',NULL,NULL,'The Menagerie','{"slug":"cleric-the-menagerie","name":"Cleric","team":"townsfolk","ability":"You start knowing a secret phrase. Once per day, if 5 or more players live and you say it publicly during a nomination, that nominee can''t die until dusk.","creator":"Goodpart","appearsIn":"The Menagerie","quote":"The power that words command can be immeasurable if chosen wisely.","lede":"The Cleric uses its words to protect its allies.","howToRun":["Consider giving the Cleric a phrase a little more obvious than what you might give a Yaggababble. The Cleric is a Townsfolk and should be in some way discernible by the evil team so that they aren''t entirely hidden."],"tips":["Your ability protects players of your choosing, so choose wisely. Unfortunately, your ability can protect evil players in the same way it can protect good ones, so learning who to trust and keeping them safe from execution is invaluable. Use your ability sparingly to ensure you aren''t caught out, and spread the good word before it''s too late."],"bluffing":["If you''re a protective role such as the Devil''s Advocate, or something that can''t die like the Lleech, your options are pretty obvious. Mask your protection - or your immunity - as the Cleric''s ability! Alternatively, if no such roles exist but you choose to bluff as the Cleric, consider mis-speaking when saying your phrase, saying it too late, or just flat out implying you''re poisoned or drunk as a ploy to insist upon your character, but not necessarily your sobriety."],"fighting":[],"examples":["Zak is the Cleric. On Night 1, he learns the phrase \"surprise Virgin!\" - Zak says this phrase when nominated, and despite a majority of votes, is not executed that day.","Idris is the Devil''s Advocate bluffing as the Cleric, using their ability to protect good players. On Night 4, they choose the Demon, state their ''phrase'', and the Demon does not die when executed."],"firstNight":16,"firstNightReminder":"Give the Cleric a secret phrase.","otherNight":0,"otherNightReminder":"","reminders":["Protected"],"setup":false,"image":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/cleg.png","curata":false,"imageAlt":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/clee.png"}','published','the-menagerie/cleric',datetime('now'),datetime('now')),
('conspiracist-the-menagerie','Conspiracist','townsfolk','Goodpart',NULL,NULL,'The Menagerie','{"slug":"conspiracist-the-menagerie","name":"Conspiracist","team":"townsfolk","ability":"You start knowing 1 player. If you are ''mad'' that they are evil, when they die, learn their alignment and that of 1 living neighbour. If you claim to be the Conspiracist, lose this ability.","creator":"Goodpart","appearsIn":"The Menagerie","quote":"Don’t you see? Don’t you see it? Look at the connections! Just look! It’s so obvious. If we assume that Mister Morozov is– no, wait… this goes deeper. This goes all the way to the top! I knew it all along!","lede":"The Conspiracist is convinced a certain player is evil, and learns the truth upon their death.","howToRun":["As the Storyteller, you choose who the Conspiracist is \"mad\" towards, and your choice matters. You can confirm neighbours of a good player, uncover an evil player, or target them directly to clear others."],"tips":["The truth is out there! You are convinced that someone in this game is definitely evil, so stick to your guns and don’t let up. Cast aspersions, nominate, spread (mis)information - whatever you need to do to convince your fellow Townsfolk that the target of your ire deserves to die. Whether they are or not is up to the Storyteller, but that’s not really the point, is it? If you maintain this madness, you’ll learn valuable information that confirms the person you’ve been mad about all game, as well as that of a living neighbour, which can go a long way to solving the game. Of course, how you do all of this is up to you, since you can’t reveal your true identity."],"bluffing":["Given that the Conspiracist can’t claim who they really are, feel free to double claim others and spread misinformation as you like: other players are likely to catch on to what you’re trying to tell them, and just might overlook the details. Additionally, should you get the player you’ve chosen executed, you then have the option to “confirm” them, and a neighbour, as good or evil. It’s possible, of course, that the player you’ve targeted may be confirmed in other ways, so don’t be too hasty to sell your world if it doesn’t align with what people already know, else you might out yourself in the process. Also note that if you have an \"expendable\" role such as a Baron, spent Assassin, Marionette, or Demon with a Scarlet Woman, you may want to target them directly, if they neighbour an evil player you want to protect."],"fighting":[],"examples":["Ann is the Conspiracist who has been informed that their chosen player is Will. Ann pushes on Will each day, and on Day 2, Will is executed. Ann learns that Will is good, and one of Ann''s neighbours is evil.","Matt is the Marionette, who is being accused of being evil by the Conspiracist. Matt is executed, and the Conspiracist learns that they are evil, but also learns that Matt''s neighbour is good. This in turn helps to clear Matt''s demon."],"firstNight":46,"firstNightReminder":"Give the Conspiracist a player''s name; give that player the *Hunch* token .","otherNight":57.5,"otherNightReminder":"If the marked player has died today or tonight, mark the Conspiracist with the *Knew All Along* token : they learn that player''s alignment, and that of one living neighbour.","reminders":["Hunch","Knew All Along","Neighbour"],"setup":false,"jinxes":[{"name":"Harpy","align":"good","text":"If the Harpy makes the Conspiracist mad at another player, the Conspiracist must be mad at both.","id":"harpy"}],"image":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/conspg.png","curata":false,"imageAlt":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/conspe.png"}','published','the-menagerie/conspiracist',datetime('now'),datetime('now')),
('daredevil-the-menagerie','Daredevil','townsfolk','Goodpart',NULL,NULL,'The Menagerie','{"slug":"daredevil-the-menagerie","name":"Daredevil","team":"townsfolk","ability":"You register as evil and the Demon to good abilities. If you are executed and either 5 players remain, or the dead equal or outnumber the living, learn the Demon is one of two players.","creator":"Goodpart","appearsIn":"The Menagerie","quote":"Living on the edge isn''t safe, but the view is certainly better.","lede":"The Daredevil appears evil and trades its survival for vital information.","howToRun":["Opt for whichever condition fits the player count: on smaller Grimoires, 5 players will remain before the dead equal the living, so pay close attention to when the Daredevil can die and still receive information.","As with the Sage, you can give the Daredevil other players that register as the Demon, should the need arise."],"tips":["Dying by execution is generally the worst way to go in Blood on the Clocktower, but the Daredevil doesn''t live by the rules - it craves execution, so long as it''s at just the right time. You register as evil and as the Demon, so town''s information will ultimately point to you - but that''s precisely what you want, isn''t it? So long as you can live just long enough, you''ll be privy to some of the most powerful information in the game, which means not only dodging town''s accusations, but the Demon, too, who may want to take you out of commission before you''re able to gather info.","With that said, there is something to be said for withholding your role, playing conservatively, and trying to steer clear of info roles that might implicate you. Confide in a select few and let them advocate for you, in the event that suspicions arise. And then, when the time is right, give town the grand reveal, getting executed in the process!"],"bluffing":["A good character who registers as an evil Demon, and can gain information on who the real Demon is when the stakes are highest? Sounds like a perfect Demon bluff - if, and only if, you have some means of carrying on with the game after you''re executed. Unlike many roles that gain information at night upon that night''s death, you don''t have the luxury of passing your demonhood to a Minion or Outsider, so a backup plan is essential if you''re going to pull off bluffing as the Daredevil. A Scarlet Woman, a Lil'' Monsta that has changed hands, or a Pit Hag who can turn an Evil Twin into a Demon are all viable fallbacks, but each come with their own distinct downsides. You''ll be trading power for information, and sway within town, so consider that before going through with your master plan."],"fighting":[],"examples":["Carla is the Daredevil. She immediately claims to her neighbour, the Gossip, and has been seen as a possible Demon by the Fortune Teller. The Gossip uses their ability to confirm the Daredevil is in play, ultimately convincing the Fortune Teller to withhold their information on Carla. On Day 4, Carla is executed, and gains her information that night.","Terry is the Ein bluffing as the Daredevil. Having been seen by multiple players as the Demon, he advocates for his own execution later in the game. He claims to learn that night that two players - neither of whom are the Zwei he has just passed to - are the Demon."],"firstNight":0,"firstNightReminder":"","otherNight":55,"otherNightReminder":"If the Daredevil was executed today and 5 players remain, or the dead equal or outnumber the living, show the Daredevil two players, one of whom is the Demon.","reminders":[],"setup":false,"image":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/infg.png","curata":false,"imageAlt":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/infe.png"}','published','the-menagerie/daredevil',datetime('now'),datetime('now')),
('dentist-the-menagerie','Dentist','townsfolk','Goodpart',NULL,NULL,'The Menagerie','{"slug":"dentist-the-menagerie","name":"Dentist","team":"townsfolk","ability":"Each night*, choose a character. You learn if they are dead.","creator":"Goodpart","appearsIn":"The Menagerie","quote":"Lying through your teeth doesn''t count as flossing.","lede":"The Dentist learns which characters are dead or alive.","howToRun":["If a character is not in play, the answer is \"no\". If multiples of a character exist, such as a Village Idiot, Lost Lover, or Fang Gu (in the event of a jump), the answer should be \"yes\", even if others of that character are alive."],"tips":["Your power comes not just from confirming the claimed roles of dead players, as an Undertaker might - you can also confirm when certain Demons may have \"jumped\" in the night. Consider who has been executed, or players who have previously died at night, and the roles they have been claiming: if you sense there''s a disparity between what a player is claiming and the information you''ve received, it''s possible that you''ve found an evil player claiming a Demon bluff. But tread lightly, as your role is a powerful one, and the evil team will be looking to neutralise you sooner rather than later."],"bluffing":["As an evil player bluffing as the Dentist, it''s up to you to sell worlds. If your Fang Gu has jumped, tell town that the role they were claiming has been seen as dead, to ensure you cover their tracks. Or perhaps you may want to discredit powerful information by noting that you''ve seen that role as alive, despite the fact that a good player is claiming to have died as that character. If they are, for instance, a Ravenkeeper who has seen an evil player as their role, you can always turn around the next day and say you checked the Ravenkeeper and received a \"no\". Doing so will help to keep suspicion off your Demon, and frame other player as necessary."],"fighting":[],"examples":["Zak is the Dentist who has received a claim stating that a player recently killed in the night was the Sage. Zak chooses the Sage the next night and learns that they are not dead, meaning that if their information is true, Zak knows that their information is false, and likely in support of evil.","Minnie is a Minion bluffing Dentist in a No Dashii game. They claim to have checked the Fang Gu and received a \"yes\". This in turn frames living Outsiders, and implies that one of the poisoned players might be a Drunk who was jumped to by the Fang Gu."],"firstNight":0,"firstNightReminder":"","otherNight":57.5,"otherNightReminder":"The Dentist selects a character.","reminders":[],"setup":false,"image":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/deng.png","curata":false,"imageAlt":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/deng.png"}','published','the-menagerie/dentist',datetime('now'),datetime('now'));